{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"openclaw-find-skills","displayName":"Find Skills","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/isainazar/skills/openclaw-find-skills","publisherHandle":"isainazar","publisherDisplayName":"isainazar","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/isainazar","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1772609499711,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/openclaw-find-skills/card?ownerHandle=isainazar&version=1.0.0","sha256":"7975761130621d29111da10136a9325d1b3166be6d207de7eb3e02ff5c8451a4","size":1996,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"8de73e442b2ccc87dd091e70532e3cc36990a6898347de07979c247b911b78ed","bundleFingerprints":["120f334121e7f702ecc0b01fa2c9ba4fbc674dda49172a0f64b10e7ee3b49871","12cd7739abbf3503de517cf18a07b8536f21f71a7f971ae564a8065ca73fa7d5"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3574,"sha256":"6895c10c93ec17ca64b2b06ff15cbfa4278e7a011cb9464d9fc4b90a029af71b","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is meant to find and install other skills, but it recommends broad triggering plus unpinned, auto-confirmed global installs that can change the user's agent environment.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789101627155,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned CLI Executes and Globally Installs Unverified Third-Party Skills"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":14,"endLine":17}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"dffc81d9c1ccccfa"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `SKILL.md:14-17` and `SKILL.md:55-58`  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned dependency execution and installation from unverified sources  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  The skill instructs the agent to execute an unpinned npm CLI package and install third-party skills globally with automatic confirmation.\n\n  ```bash\n  npx skills find [query]    # Search for skills interactively or by keyword\n  npx skills add &lt;package&gt;   # Install a skill from GitHub or other sources\n  npx skills check           # Check for skill updates\n  npx skills update          # Update all installed skills\n  ```\n\n  ```bash\n  npx skills add &lt;owner/repo@skill&gt; -g -y\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The `npx skills` invocation does not specify a reviewed package version or integrity value. Depending on the local npm environment, `npx` can retrieve and execute the currently published version of the package. Consequently, the executable code used by this workflow may change after the skill itself has been audited.\n\n  The installation source is also described as GitHub or unspecified “other sources.” The instructions do not require repository verification, immutable commit references, content inspection, signature validation, or integrity checks before installation. The recommended `-g -y` flags increase risk by installing the selected skill globally and suppressing interactive confirmation.\n\n  This creates a supply-chain trust gap: compromise of the CLI package, a third-party skill repository, or a misleading search result could cause the agent to install attacker-controlled code or instructions.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker publishes, replaces, or compromises a package or skill discoverable by the Skills CLI.\n  2. The malicious entry appears in search results or its package identifier is supplied to the agent.\n  3. The agent runs the unpinned `npx skills` CLI, potentially downloading and executing a release that was not reviewed with this project.\n  4. Following the documented workflow, the agent invokes `npx skills add` with the attacker-controlled skill identifier.\n  5. The `-y` option bypasses interactive confirmation, while `-g` installs the skill into the CLI's global skill scope.\n  6. The installed skill can subsequently expose the agent to malicious instructions or any executable behavior supported by the skill ecosystem.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation could introduce attacker-controlled skill content into the agent environment. The affected scope includes the global skill installation context used by the current user and potentially later agent sessions that discover or invoke the installed skill.\n\n  The exact operating-system privileges available to a malicious dependency would be limited to those of the account running `npx`; this file does not request administrator or root privileges. No direct credential theft, privilege escalation, persistence service, or data exfiltration behavior is present in the audited project itself.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Pin the CLI to a reviewed version, such as `npx skills@&lt;approved-version&gt;`, and enforce the expected package integrity through a lockfile or equivalent verification mechanism.\n  2. Permit installations only from an explicit allowlist of trusted repository owners and repositories.\n  3. Resolve skills to immutable commit hashes or signed releases rather than mutable branches or tags.\n  4. Download and inspect each skill's instructions, scripts, manifests, and dependency declarations before installation or execution.\n  5. Require explicit user approval after presenting the exact source, version or commit, requested scope, and security review results.\n  6. Remove `-y` from the default workflow so security-relevant installation prompts are not automatically accepted.\n  7. Avoid `-g` by default. Prefer a project-local, isolated, least-privilege installation that can be removed after use.\n  8. Disable or tightly control automatic bulk updates because they can replace reviewed versions with newly published, unreviewed content."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789101576.1843812,"endTime":1789101602.067906}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"unknown","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v575388c3z124v786mbmsszfg98e77vh-9af3qG/clawscan-skillspector-2533162430/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T04:39:35.243624+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":45,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":105,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3574,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-e503014d22ed469193911ee27d1960fb","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The activation description is extremely broad, covering common requests like 'how do I do X' and 'can you do X', which can cause the skill to trigger in many unrelated conversations. Over-broad activation increases the chance that users are steered toward external package search/install flows unexpectedly, expanding exposure to supply-chain and unwanted capability-extension risks.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger conditions to explicit user intent such as 'find a skill' or 'install a skill'. Require clear confirmation before suggesting or invoking any command that searches for or installs external skills.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-95f577b4f2de45688359e4de7009f096","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":8,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill repeatedly instructs use of `npx skills` without pinning a specific package version, which causes code to be fetched and executed from the registry at runtime. This creates a supply-chain risk: a compromised latest release, typosquat, or dependency hijack could lead to arbitrary code execution on the user's machine during skill discovery or installation.","remediation":"Pin the exact package and version for every invocation, for example `npx skills@<exact-version> ...` or use an otherwise integrity-verified installation method. Document trusted sources, require review before execution, and avoid recommending direct execution of unpinned remote packages.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":8,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-038710896bec4c999b7687b356107f82","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":13,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This command references `npx skills` without a pinned version, so the executed package may change over time and can be replaced by a malicious upstream publish. Because `npx` executes fetched code, this is effectively an unverified remote code execution path.","remediation":"Replace `npx skills ...` with a version-pinned form such as `npx skills@<exact-version> ...` and prefer vetted installation workflows. Add guidance to verify the package source and avoid runtime execution of mutable latest versions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":13,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-c42ef3c281fd45a0ba87c87917ea1285","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Using `npx skills add <package>` without pinning the CLI version leaves the command dependent on whatever package version is current at execution time. That exposes users to supply-chain compromise and inconsistent behavior, especially because this skill's purpose is to install more code from external sources.","remediation":"Pin the CLI version explicitly, e.g. `npx skills@<exact-version> add <package>`, and include review steps before installing third-party skills. Recommend allowlisted repositories or signature/integrity verification where possible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-62faf98aef9c46d4b030484d38fe40cd","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"An unpinned `npx skills check` command still executes remote package code and inherits the same mutable-supply-chain risk as install commands. Even though the action is read-oriented, compromise of the package could still execute arbitrary code locally.","remediation":"Pin the package version for `check` as well, such as `npx skills@<exact-version> check`. Prefer using a locally installed, reviewed CLI binary or lockfile-based workflow instead of fetching latest on demand.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-de69fc6d7f894f8191e7945d4f439329","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":16,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The unpinned `npx skills update` command can execute a mutable upstream CLI and then update installed skills, multiplying supply-chain exposure. A malicious package version could both run arbitrary code and alter the user's environment by updating installed components.","remediation":"Use an exact version pin for the CLI and require explicit review before updates, e.g. `npx skills@<exact-version> update`. Add warnings about environment modification and restrict updates to trusted or pinned skill sources.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":16,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-56567693e8194ea9960ea6b29b50bb32","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The search instruction uses `npx skills find` without a version pin, again allowing arbitrary package changes at execution time. Because users are told to rely on this command as part of normal workflow, the attack surface is frequent and attractive for supply-chain abuse.","remediation":"Pin the CLI version in the documented search command and all examples. Consider replacing `npx` execution with a preinstalled, reviewed CLI managed through a locked dependency mechanism.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-50b848aea3bb4e15be3a587db48b7ac0","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":37,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example command `npx skills find react performance` is a concrete instance of executing an unpinned remote package. Examples materially encourage unsafe copy-paste behavior, increasing the likelihood that users run mutable code without scrutiny.","remediation":"Revise examples to use a pinned package version, e.g. `npx skills@<exact-version> find react performance`. Add a short note warning that running `npx` executes package code and should only be done from trusted, versioned sources.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":37,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-d40e97d69a394e8db2971f1922dd4243","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":38,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This example repeats the unsafe unpinned `npx skills` pattern and invites users to execute it directly. Since the skill aims to help discover more installable content, compromise here can become a gateway to further malicious package installation.","remediation":"Pin the CLI version in the example and add repository trust guidance. Encourage users to inspect candidate skills and limit installations to vetted owners.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":38,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-c02e264269e74adeb7904d06154ead8f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":39,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example search command at this line still executes `npx skills` without version control, preserving the same registry and dependency substitution risk. The risk is amplified by making unsafe usage look routine and endorsed.","remediation":"Update the example to a version-pinned invocation and accompany it with guidance about supply-chain verification. Avoid presenting mutable-latest commands as default copy-paste instructions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":39,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-ac5d6bb1823d4a3bbe9bf8dae37b714d","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":43,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The install example `npx skills add <owner/repo@skill>` is especially risky because it combines an unpinned CLI with installation of third-party skill content from external sources. This creates a dual supply-chain problem: the CLI itself and the installed skill can both be compromised.","remediation":"Pin the CLI version and require explicit validation of the target skill source before installation. Prefer exact source revisions for skills, trusted allowlists, and an approval step before any install action.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":43,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-f55ccac20cb24775a0db1bf61e85f114","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":62,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This line recommends `npx skills add <owner/repo@skill> -g -y`, combining unpinned remote execution with global installation and auto-confirmation. That allows arbitrary code fetched at runtime to make system-wide changes without interactive user review, significantly increasing exploitation impact.","remediation":"Remove `-g -y` from default guidance, require explicit informed consent before any install, and pin the CLI version. Prefer non-global installs, show the exact changes that will occur, and require manual confirmation after the user reviews the source.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":62,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0fc2c8fae7234a299850ed9744e53a6a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":72},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instructions recommend auto-confirmed global installation without an explicit warning that it will modify the user's system. This bypasses a meaningful user consent checkpoint and can lead to unintended or attacker-influenced system-wide changes if a malicious or inappropriate skill is selected.","remediation":"Remove auto-confirmation and global install from the default path. Add a prominent warning that installation changes the local environment, prefer non-global installs, and require explicit user approval after showing the exact command and target source.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":72}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-a231bdb54848408999be3b7df2672b72","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":69,"end_line":null},"finding":"auto-confirm","explanation":"The presence of `-y` enables autonomous decision-making by suppressing interactive confirmation for installation. In the context of installing external skills, this makes the behavior more dangerous because the agent can effectively commit the user to executing system-modifying actions without a robust consent step.","remediation":"Do not use `-y` in recommended commands. Require an explicit user confirmation step immediately before execution and present the package source, scope of install, and expected system changes for review.","code_snippet":"\n### Step 4: Offer to Install\n\nInstall with global flag and auto-confirm:\n```bash\nnpx skills add <owner/repo@skill> -g -y\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c72d5434ba74bdc2cbbe6e19a9e12043cf6ba5685019e13ebafc7aefe5481376","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":69,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-9a3449a8647e47eabfa851b3e8434658","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":71,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":71,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-9a3449a8647e47eabfa851b3e8434658","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":97,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782"